WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.136
-From Studio 60
in Rockefeller Center

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.071
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.806
it's a special
five-minute edition

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.342
of "The Tonight Show"
starring Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.777
It's the "Fallon Five."

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:18.751
And now, here's your host,
Jimmy Fallon!

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.787
-♪ Hey, hey hey, hey ♪

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.522
-♪ Hey, hey hey, hey ♪

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:27.860
-♪ Hey, hey hey, hey ♪

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.997
-Thank you very much!
Please, welcome, welcome!

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.431
Thank you.
Please stop clapping.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:33.633
We only have five minutes.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.068
We're already --
The show's already over.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:38.471
Uh, Paul Rudd will be out here
in a little bit

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.106
but first, here's
what people are talking about.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:44.444
You guys, today is day 11
of the 2018 Winter Olympics!

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.445
Now...

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.782
...while it is day 12
of Fergie's National Anthem

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.351
at the NBA All-Star game.
-Hey-oh!

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.154
-It's still going on.
It's still going on now.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.722
Yeah.
Did you see this?

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.657
Everybody is talking about this.
At the NBA All-Star game

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:01.728
last night, Fergie performed a
pretty interesting rendition

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.896
of the National Anthem.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:05.932
It was a pretty
creative take on the song.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.233
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.667
Just watch the players'
reactions -- This is real.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.704
-♪ Gave proof ♪

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.607
♪ Through the night ♪

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:21.980
♪ That our flag
was still there ♪

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.318
♪ Oh, oh, say ♪

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:39.098
♪ Does that star-spangled
banner-er ye-yet wave ♪

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:45.971
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:48.374
-I don't wanna say it was rough,
but even Trump took a knee.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.376
I mean, that's when you're like,
you know, she's that bad.

00:01:51.376 --> 00:01:52.511
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:53.880
-[ As Trump ] Wall.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.516
I saw that German figure skater
Paul Fentz went viral

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.851
when he did his free skate to
music from "Game of Thrones."

00:01:58.851 --> 00:01:59.886
Take a look at this.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.921
♪♪

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:07.860
Yeah, pretty cool.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.462
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.397
It worked even better when
he tried using another

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.099
TV show theme song.
Watch this.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.469
<i> -Next up, representing Germany,
 Paul Fentz.</i>

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.571
-♪ Who lives in a pineapple
under the sea ♪

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.539
-♪ Spongebob Squarepants ♪

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.608
-♪ Absorbent and yellow
and porous is he ♪

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:24.711
-♪ Spongebob Squarepants ♪

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.546
[ Applause ]

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.147
-Spongebob!

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.382
Ooh, a bit of a scandal.
A bit of a scandal here.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:33.119
A member of the Russian curling
team failed a drug test

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.754
and is being accused
of cheating.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.055
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.191
Now, I don't really know
if doping would really affect

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.159
the outcome of a sport
like curling, but --

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.461
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.829
Take a look at this guy.
Watch this.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.865
<i> [ Audience applauding ]</i>

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.132
[ Explosion ]

00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:49.201
Just a little bit.
You know, it's unfair.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:50.403
It's unfair.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.638
Another big story right now
is U.S. Hockey.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.106
The women are going
for the gold,

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:57.109
while the men are close
to being eliminated.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.512
Which also kind of sums up
the year 2018.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.981
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.981 --> 00:03:05.952
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:13.526
[ Playing Queen's
"Under Pressure" ]

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.727
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:18.797
Now, our show tonight is
only five minutes long,

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:22.568
which means we don't have enough
time for a normal interview.

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.904
But that won't stop me, no.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.773
I still want to make sure that
we give you guys everything

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.441
that you'd normally get
so with that in mind,

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:31.443
it is time for the
first-ever "Tonight Show"

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.713
one-minute interview.
Here we go.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.082
-♪ One-minute interview ♪

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.150
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.617 line:0%
-I'm going to do an entire
interview

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.386 line:0%
with tonight's guest
in just one minute,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.588 line:0%
so let's put 60 seconds
on the clock.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.290 line:0%
Ready?
Here we go.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.359 line:0%
Our guest tonight is a very
funny, very talented actor.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.494 line:0%
His new movie "Mute" comes out
on Netflix this Friday.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.496 line:0%
Everyone, please welcome back
a friend of the show, Paul Rudd!

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:55.602 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.270 line:0%
Oh, my goodness.
Paul, great to see you.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.671 line:0%
How is it going?
-Really good.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.173 line:0%
-The Winter Olympics are
happening right now.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.541 line:0%
Have you been watching those?
-I have been -- it's great.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.642 line:0%
-What is your favorite Olympic
sport?

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:06.345 line:0%
-Well, I love skiing, but --
-Do you consider yourself...

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.381 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.049 line:0%
...athletic, an athletic person?

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.784 line:0%
I like sports a lot.
I played soccer when I was --

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.587 line:0%
-Let's talk about your new
movie, "Mute."

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.123 line:0%
Can you tell us a little bit
about it?

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.058 line:0%
-It's kind of a sci-fi --
-That's more than enough.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.126 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.661 line:0%
Do you wear a mustache in the
film?

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.062 line:0%
-I do.
-What was that like?

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.398 line:0%
-Crazy.
-Let's take a look at a clip

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.498 line:0%
from "Mute."

00:04:26.498 --> 00:04:27.866 line:0%
<i> -Don't do that again.</i>

00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:29.202 line:0%
-That looks great.
Hey, do you want to sing?

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:30.203 line:0%
-Yes.
-Oh, perfect.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.204 line:0%
Let's sing a song right now.

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.840 line:0%
-♪ You know you make me want
to shout ♪

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.175 line:0%
♪ Kick my heels up and shout,
throw my hands up and shout ♪

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.377 line:0%
♪ Throw my head back and shout ♪

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.446 line:0%
♪ A little bit lower now, shout,
a little bit lower now, shout ♪

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.448 line:0%
♪ A little bit louder now
a little bit louder now ♪

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.116 line:0%
♪ Hey ♪

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:45.818 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]
Thank you very much, Paul Rudd!

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.286
Catch "Mute" on Netflix
this Friday.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.755
Thank you for watching.
Have a great night.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.656
Hope to see you tomorrow.
Bye-bye, everybody!

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:59.265
[ The Roots continue
playing "Shout" ]

